page 1 (
    name: Create experiment
    alias: CREATE
    title: Create | Genesis Living Control
    appearance {
        pageTemplate: @/standard
        templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    }
    security {
        authentication: required
        pageAccessProtection: argumentsMustHaveChecksum
    }
    region create-request (
        name: Create bounded experiment
        type: staticContent
        layout {
            sequence: 10
            slot: body
            columnSpan: 12
            startNewRow: true
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/standard
            templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
        }
        source {
            htmlCode: ```html
<section id="living-control" class="lc" data-control-page="create">
 <nav class="lc-steps" aria-label="Application evolution"><a href="f?p=&APP_ID.:1:&APP_SESSION." aria-current="page"><span>01</span> Create</a><a href="f?p=&APP_ID.:2:&APP_SESSION."><span>02</span> Evolve</a><a href="f?p=&APP_ID.:3:&APP_SESSION."><span>03</span> Watch</a></nav>
 <header class="lc-intro"><p class="lc-eyebrow">APEX GENESIS / LIVING APPLICATIONS</p><h1>Every application<br><span>starts with a question.</span></h1><p>Name a bounded Order Lab experiment. Genesis will create a parent, test a structural variation, and let Oracle decide what survives.</p></header>
 <p data-status class="lc-status" role="status">Control is disabled or not configured.</p>
 <div class="lc-create-grid"><div class="lc-panel"><h2>Create your experiment</h2><p class="lc-muted">Create saves an immutable draft. Start Evolution queues that draft for an authorized worker.</p>
 <label class="lc-field">Experiment label <input name="label" maxlength="120" required disabled placeholder="What would you like to explore?"></label>
 <p class="lc-capability">One generation <span>·</span> Two applications <span>·</span> No AI requests</p>
 <button class="lc-primary" type="button" data-action="CREATE" disabled>Create draft</button>
 <details class="lc-details"><summary>Experiment limits</summary><p>These fixed limits keep the first feasibility protocol reproducible. They cannot be expanded from this screen.</p><div class="lc-limits"><label>Random seed <input name="seed" type="number" min="50000" max="50000" value="50000" readonly required disabled></label><label>Challenger generations <input name="generations" type="number" min="1" max="1" value="1" readonly required disabled></label><label>Application materialization budget <input name="materializationBudget" type="number" min="2" max="2" value="2" readonly required disabled></label></div><p>GA_ONLY · fixed synthetic tasks · engineering proxy fitness.</p></details></div>
 <aside class="lc-method"><p class="lc-eyebrow">WHAT WILL BE TESTED</p><ol><li><strong>Locate</strong><span>Find the intended order.</span></li><li><strong>Filter</strong><span>Narrow the report to the requested records.</span></li><li><strong>Update</strong><span>Change the intended record and verify persistence.</span></li></ol><p>Task success needs observed evidence. A generated application has not yet passed a test.</p></aside></div>
 <div class="lc-request-bar"><label>Existing requests <select data-requests disabled></select></label></div>
 <div data-observation></div>
 <footer class="lc-footer">B2DEV TECH / INDEPENDENT RESEARCH <span>0.3 development</span></footer>
</section>
            ```
        }
    )
    process living-control (
        name: LIVING_CONTROL
        type: executeCode
        source {
            plsqlCode: ```plsql
apxgen_app_control.ajax;
            ```
        }
        execution {
            sequence: 10
            point: ajaxCallback
        }
    )
)
